  (text "1. Mains entry and outlet feeds" (at 15.24 25.4 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 2438192b-a449-4095-a2ef-a9bb78fab58a))
  (text "Ring L/N/E land on the busbar; only outlet current passes the shunts and relays.\nShunt common end = L_BUS = hot-side ground. Route IP/IN as Kelvin taps from the shunt pads.\nThermal cut-offs: non-resettable, clamped to the outlet feed near the contacts; Tf chosen after the EVT thermal test." (at 15.24 29.21 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 1f0e8ab8-8334-464f-b664-a6ea41c16317))
  (text "2. Electronics feed and surge protection" (at 15.24 67.31 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid c0997479-4032-482c-8893-7802334285e9))
  (text "Fuse and series resistor per Mornsun's LD03 application circuit. MOV after the fuse, thermally protected type.\nOpen item: the MOV clamp (~925 V at 25 A for 561K) exceeds the KP3310 drain rating (650 V). See review notes R1." (at 15.24 71.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 54932f99-7fe2-4a80-9cf6-a5da2ac6f917))
  (text "3. Hot-side 3.3 V supply (KP3310SGA)" (at 15.24 100.33 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid fb5c4bd2-0e5f-40f6-94b1-819fe15fa6a1))
  (text "Half-wave from N_F; KP3310 charges VDD (7.8 V) while the line is low, then an LDO makes 3.3 V. SEL open = 3.3 V.\nHold-up: 15 mA (worst case) x 20 ms / 220 uF = 1.4 V droop on VDD (7.8 V to 6.4 V), so VOUT stays in regulation." (at 15.24 104.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0d85ace0-58bb-444d-8c25-a2d24cf9aa48))
  (text "4. Metering (BL0939)" (at 15.24 140.97 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 416d085e-5225-45bd-a272-00cfc1c95f4e))
  (text "UART address 5 (A1, A3 high; A2, A4 low): the firmware sends 0x55/0xA5, which encode address 5.\nDivider 5 x 390k + 470R: 230 V gives 55 mV rms, 290 V gives 70 mV rms (pin limit 70 mV rms). Firmware board file: div_r_bottom = 0.47 k.\nAlarms: CF (channel A, MODE[12]) OR I_LEAK (channel B) -> isolator channel E. Both active high." (at 15.24 144.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 670f6c58-8181-4966-a678-ac0e0e74389e))
  (text "5. Polarity and earth check" (at 15.24 220.98 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 806266cc-db22-4804-a03d-72b55c732786))
  (text "Arm A: E -> 2 x 2M (HV) -> sense 20k -> L_BUS.  Arm B: E -> 2 x 2M (HV) + 20k -> N_F, so a missing earth floats to mid-supply.\nPeak detector BAT54WS + 1u // 1M (tau 1 s); thresholds 1.02 V (bit A) and 0.31 V (bit B) from a 220k/68k/30k ladder.\nCorrect: A=1 B=1.  Swapped L/N: A=0 B=0.  No earth: A=0 B=1.  Each arm must withstand a 6 kV impulse: VR37-class HV resistors." (at 15.24 224.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid b73d77d8-c70f-464c-82cc-bd159aa5e2f1))
